{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "03 An app action, click to result",
  "description": "A person clicks an action in an app (the synthetic contract fixture in hive/plugins/contract_fixture). Follow it through the UI, the program action route, visibility, identity and confirm checks, the app's own act(), result validation and the view refresh. Lines were read at this repository's handover commit; if a line has moved, search the file for the step's function or symbol name.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "hive/plugins/contract_fixture/plugin.json",
      "line": 8,
      "title": "1. The app declares what it may do",
      "description": "Every app ships a manifest. `capabilities` lists the hive powers it may use; this fixture asks only for `goals:write`. The host refuses any other power at the moment it is used (step 12). The fixture is invented test data."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/plugins/contract_fixture/program.py",
      "line": 36,
      "title": "2. The app declares its actions",
      "description": "`describe()` returns the contract: item kinds, relations and **actions**. Each action says which kinds it applies to and which params it takes. The host only ever delivers an action named here."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/ui/src/features/programs/ProgramHost.tsx",
      "line": 130,
      "title": "3. The click",
      "description": "The generic app host renders the app's view. Choosing an action calls `act(key, action, ids)`. `act` comes from `useConfirmedProgramAct` (line 77): actions that need a host confirm open the host's own dialog first; the others go straight to the store."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/ui/src/store/store.ts",
      "line": 1201,
      "title": "4. store.programAct",
      "description": "Marks the session busy, adds the person's current focus and stage to the params, and sends the action with the view's `base_revision` (line 1212). The revision lets the app say \"stale\" if the view changed meanwhile."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/ui/src/api/live.ts",
      "line": 449,
      "title": "5. POST /api/programs/{id}/act",
      "description": "One request to the host."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/app.py",
      "line": 2899,
      "title": "6. The route",
      "description": "The body is streamed with a size cap. Three checks run **before the app is called**: the person may see the swarm, every mind named in the request is one they may see, and the request does not try to set who acts or carry a credential. Then the host builds the actor itself from the session."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/visibility.py",
      "line": 299,
      "title": "7. Visibility checks",
      "description": "`check_path` refuses a swarm, mind or goal the person may not see as **not found**, so existence is not revealed. `check_named_minds` (line 281) scans every decoded string for `mind:<id>` or `agent:<id>` under a bounded budget, and refuses when the scan cannot finish."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/program_actions.py",
      "line": 119,
      "title": "8. Identity and credentials are the host's",
      "description": "`refuse_identity` rejects identity fields and anything that looks like a key or credential in the body or params. Apps hold their own credentials; the hive sets who acts."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/program_actions.py",
      "line": 381,
      "title": "9. person_act: approver and confirm binding",
      "description": "Looks up the declared action. An action with `approver: person` needs a named signed-in person, not the local operator password. An action that needs a confirm must present a single-use token bound to the person, session, app, swarm, action and payload digest (`_take_confirm`, line 360). The fixture's actions declare no confirm and no `person_activity`, so they take the direct path at line 408."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/programs.py",
      "line": 825,
      "title": "10. Is the app ready?",
      "description": "`_ready` refuses an app that failed to load, is not its pinned release (`HIVE_APP_PINS`), or is disabled. It re-checks source integrity on every view, act, result check and UI bundle."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/programs.py",
      "line": 1053,
      "title": "11. Programs.act",
      "description": "Refuses an action the app did not declare. Builds a `ProgramContext` for this swarm, with the host's actor and command record. `_call` (line 885) runs the app's `view` or `act`, sync or async (`describe` is called once at load and must be sync, line 680). A `PermissionError` becomes 403 `program_refused`, an error that carries its own status passes through, and any other crash becomes a clean 500 `program_error` (lines 893-900)."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/plugins/contract_fixture/program.py",
      "line": 116,
      "title": "12. The app's own act()",
      "description": "The app does its own work. It returns `stale` if `base_revision` is old, and `refused` without targets. `challenge` and `investigate-gap` post a goal through `ctx.create_goal`, which checks the declared capability (`hive/core/programs.py` lines 290 and 113). `correct` keeps ids, records the prior revision and flags the conclusions that depend on it."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/programs.py",
      "line": 1295,
      "title": "13. The result is validated",
      "description": "Whatever the app returns must have a known `status`. A `graph` is checked against the app's own declared kinds and relations. A receipt must have a known state. A `started` action must return a task id or a pending receipt, so its progress can be followed."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/ui/src/store/programSession.ts",
      "line": 292,
      "title": "14. The page applies the result",
      "description": "Every result replaces the last one's data, so a stale or failed action never leaves earlier data looking current. `done` with a graph moves the view; `started` reloads goals (`hive/ui/src/store/store.ts` line 1220)."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/ui/src/store/store.ts",
      "line": 1156,
      "title": "15. The view refresh",
      "description": "When the result asks for it, `programRefresh` reads the view again through `POST /api/programs/{id}/view`, which runs the same visibility checks (`hive/core/app.py` line 2875). A sequence number drops answers that arrive out of order. Known gap: there is no single guided flow yet to deploy an app with its swarm (see `STATUS.md`)."
    }
  ]
}
